    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22495" root="شعر" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَشْعَرٌ</span></b>  <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَعْلَمٌ</span> [meaning <i>A place where a
thing is known to be</i>]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And hence, <i>A
place of the performance of religious services.</i>
(TA.) See this word, and its pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَشَاعِرُ</span>, voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شِعَارٌ</span>,
in four places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  [The pl.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المَشَاعِرُ</span> also signifies
<i>The five senses;</i> (S, * A, * TA;) <i>the hearing, the
sight, the smell, the taste, and the touch.</i> (S and
Msb in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حس</span>.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَعَارٌ</span>.

